# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LedgerLock — .gitignore
#
# NOTE ON WHAT IS *NOT* IGNORED (deliberate, per project-statement.md §12):
#   results.md              the metrics table — root level, non-negotiable
#   exceptions.md           the honest unresolved list
#   runs/run_log.jsonl      full audit trail; `make run` replays every verdict from it
#   runs/analyst_cache.jsonl    recorded LLM responses — makes the run reproducible
#                               with no API key and no network
#   runs/analyst_provider.json  which provider/model produced that cache
#   data/*.csv              seed-42 output; committed so a judge can read the mess
#                           without running anything. `make data` regenerates them
#                           byte-identically.
#   uv.lock                 pins the viewer's dependencies; the engine has none
# These are the submission. Do not add them below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Secrets — API keys are read from the environment only, never from a flag.
# Nothing here should ever reach a commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch — local experiments, not part of the submission
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
